      "text": "Given the point of intersection $(6, 10)$, we can substitute these values into each equation to get two linear equations in terms of $m$ and $b$.\n\nFor the first equation ($y = mx + 4$):\n\\begin{align*}\n10 &= 6m + 4 \\\\\nm &= \\frac{10 - 4}{6} \\\\\nm &= \\frac{6}{6} \\\\\nm &= 1\n\\end{align*}\n\nFor the second equation ($y = 3x + b$):\n\\begin{align*}\n10 &= 3(6) + b \\\\\n10 &= 18 + b \\\\\nb &= 10 - 18 \\\\\nb &= -8\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, we can find the value of $b + m$:\n\\begin{align*}\nb + m &= (-8) + 1 \\\\\n&= -7\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, the value of $b + m$ is $\\boxed{-7}$.",
